{"_notes":["Locally added -- upstream pinmame-nvram-maps has no X-Men map as of index rev 1406.","Records are 0x20 apart, NUL-terminated initials at +0x00, a 4-byte little-endian score at","+0x18, and a 16-bit checksum in the last two bytes of the first 30 -- the same record shape","the other Stern SAM maps use. The checksum verifies on all six records and fails on the","seventh, which is what bounds the block.","Confirmed against two cabinets: one still on Stern's factory ladder (75M/55M/40M/30M/25M","with 'G S'/'L R'/'J R'/'D T'/'P P'), the other with real play on it.","The sixth record is the Combo Champion, read off the machine's own champion display.","game on 24 (same platform), where a 4-byte stride reads player 2 as zero and player 3's","score as player 2's.","over from the verified 24 layout: no 3- or 4-player game has been played on either machine, and","In-progress scores are 4 bytes on 4-byte centres, verified by a 2-player game reading","3,119,500 and 4,467,600 at 0x021109E4 and 0x021109E8. Players 3 and 4 have not been observed:","no 3- or 4-player game has been played, and those bytes still sit inside a 0xFF fill the","firmware has never written.","player_count at 0x02110900 is verified on this ROM: it reads 1 after a 1-player game and 2 after","a 2-player one, and 24 uses the same address, so that field at least is shared across SAM games.","current_ball is at 0x00030AE5, in CPU RAM rather than NVRAM, identified by how it moves rather","than what it reads: across a whole game it stepped 1->2->3 and nothing else, with the score","climbing between the steps. Five exit snapshots had failed to find it, and the one other address","that survived those (0x0002FB20) turned out to cycle 0,1,2,5,4,3,2,1,4 -- a display value.","It is not the address 24 uses, which reads 16 here, nor does it mean anything on LUCI, which","reads 0. Like the score base and stride, the ball counter is per-ROM on SAM.","volume at 0x02110250 read 60 across four earlier captures and 40 after the operator set it to 40","on a 0-63 scale -- the only byte in the 128K that changed that way, so no second capture was","needed to confirm it.","current_player is the byte immediately below the ball, at 0x00030AE4. In a 4-player game it","completed 1->2->3 three times -- once per ball, as player-up rotating through four players does --","against one completion for the ball, and the two interlock: the ball stepped at the same scores","the player cycles finished at.","The four scores of that game read 721,760 / 1,099,300 / 853,880 / 1,302,140 exactly where this map","declares them, so the 4-byte stride is measured here rather than carried over from another ROM.","Only xmn_151h is claimed: the other X-Men revisions were not checked and SAM high score","addresses move between ROM revisions.","game_over, tilted, credits and volume come from a 714-frame recording of live memory spanning","an operator-menu session and one five-ball game with a mid-ball tilt on ball 1. The menu session","also promoted ball_count and max_credits from derived to measured: Balls Per Game 3 -> 5 landed","at adjustment index 30 and Max Credits 30 -> 9 at index 32, as the free_play-relative rule","predicted. Ball Save Timer 5 -> 0 landed at index 37, four records above free play; it is not","a mapped field but the position is the same on every SAM game measured.","0x00030B16 is the status bitfield SAM games keep at ball+0x31, in its plainest variant: 1 in","attract, 19 in play, 21 for exactly the nine samples between the tilt and the end of the","tilted ball, during which player 1's score sat frozen at 45,630. game_over is mask 0x12","inverted, correct in all 714 frames; tilted is bit 0x04.","volume at 0x02110250, set from 60 to 58 in the operator menu with its complement check byte","following; declared as checksum8. credits at 0x0211100C, the twentieth SAM game at that","address, stepping up with each coin and down once at game start.","2026-11: game_over is mask 0xFE inverted and tilted the value 0x15 over mask 0x7F on 0x00030B16:","mask 0x12 took the mode value 28 for game over, bit 0x04 is set in 4F/55/67, and 55 equals 15","under 0x1F.","2026-11: The A.1 (64) and A.2 (47) adjustments added from the ROM image (README, 'Adjustments","from the ROM').","Confirmed on a cabinet 2026-11-13 (ALP4K; two players, tilt on P1 ball 1): 538,320 / 667,290,","the records and the status byte matched the DMD."],"_fileformat":0.9,"_metadata":{"version":16,"license":"Open Data Commons Open Database License (ODbL) v1.0","copyright":["Copyright (C) 2026 by Wes Smith <evilwraith@gmail.com>"],"platform":"stern-sam.6e326d93","roms":["xmn_151h"],"validation":{"checksum":[{"_notes":"117 adjustments: 4-byte LE value, 1-byte checksum, 3 bytes 0xFF padding","label":"Adjustment {#} (checksum)","start":"0x02102008","length":5,"complement":true,"repeat":{"count":117,"step":8}},{"label":"Master Volume","start":"0x2110250","end":"0x2110251","complement":true},{"label":"Champion record {#} (checksum)","start":"0x2103000","repeat":{"count":6,"step":32},"length":30,"bits":16,"complement":true}]},"values":{"no_yes":["NO","YES"],"credit_ticket_token":["CREDIT","TICKET","TOKEN"]}},"checksum8":[{"label":"Free Play adjustment","start":"0x02102110","end":"0x02102114"},{"label":"Balls Per Game adjustment","start":"0x021020F8","end":"0x021020FC"},{"label":"Maximum Credits adjustment","start":"0x02102108","end":"0x0210210C"},{"label":"Master Volume","start":"0x02110250","end":"0x02110251"}],"game_state":{"player_count":{"label":"Player Count","encoding":"int","start":"0x02110900"},"free_play":{"label":"Free Play","encoding":"bool","start":"0x02102110"},"credits":{"label":"Credits","encoding":"int","start":"0x0211100C"},"volume":{"label":"Volume","encoding":"int","start":"0x02110250","min":0,"max":63,"default":40},"max_credits":{"label":"Maximum Credits","encoding":"int","start":"0x02102108"},"ball_count":{"label":"Balls Per Game","encoding":"int","start":"0x021020F8"},"current_player":{"